  "notes": "2004 mixed-use residential block on the Folsom S frontage between the mid-block tower and the 4th Street corner (DataSF footprint, no OSM way). Pale blue-grey render upper storeys with a regular grid of paired white-framed windows; charcoal ground storey of shopfronts between square piers, each under a deep maroon fabric awning; a glazed residential lobby door; flat parapet cap. Pale blue-teal render (was lavender-grey reading), reflective window glass (glassModel), smooth-render weathering. The render tint read sage/teal in the street light (painted-stucco's warm albedo x a teal tint). Tint re-derived bluer; coping to match. Upper windows too sparse, awnings read as a red trim strip, ground too uniformly black. Windows every 1.6 m at 1.0 m wide; awnings 1.3 m deep with a 0.6 m valance; ground a lighter charcoal. Awnings read as flat strips; sloped fabric awnings (1.0 m rise over the 1.3 m depth, kit riseM/dropM); paler blue-grey render. No awnings over the SW end of the front; lighter charcoal base; windows set deeper. Each awning span split into two discrete awnings with a gap, lower rise, so they read as separate fabric awnings not one band. Wall greyer pale blue (was periwinkle), lighter ground band (was blue-black), window reveals 0.45 m.",
